# A MISSING hashed build asset must 404, NOT fall through to the SPA catch-all
# below. Without this rule, a request for a chunk that a newer deploy has purged
# (or that hasn't finished propagating to this edge yet) matches `/*` and comes
# back as index.html with a 200 — HTML where the browser expected a JS module.
# A dynamic import() then throws (in Safari, a TypeError with a null stack), and
# far worse under the immutable Cache-Control on /assets/* (see public/_headers),
# the browser caches that broken HTML response for a YEAR, so even a reload can't
# recover. A real 404 keeps the failure clean and uncacheable: import() fails,
# the vite:preloadError handler reloads once, and the retry gets real JS (or a
# clean 404 again). Cloudflare serves existing static files before consulting
# this file, so real assets are unaffected — only genuinely-missing ones 404.
/assets/*   /404.html   404

# SPA fallback: every path with no matching static file renders the app shell.
# NOTE: do NOT add explicit /terms -> /terms.html or /privacy -> /privacy.html
# rewrites here. Cloudflare Pages serves static files first and exposes them at
# their extensionless URL automatically (/privacy.html is reachable at /privacy),
# and it 308-redirects /privacy.html -> /privacy on its own. An explicit
# /privacy -> /privacy.html rewrite fights that auto-redirect and causes an
# infinite 308 loop. Static-first + the catch-all below is all that's needed.
/*    /index.html   200
